.git/ is not a typical place for a working file, but the alternatives
are worse. A file in the worktree needs a .gitignore entry, and the
host repo has not agreed to add one. A temp file outside the repo
disappears before anyone can check the score. Git already keeps
COMMIT_EDITMSG in .git/ for the same reason.

The draft file stays after the commit finishes. This costs nothing, and
gives git commit --amend -F a starting point if the message needs a
fix.
